{"type":"message","id":"14d6234f","parentId":"ceba8062","timestamp":"2026-03-13T17:24:28.669Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"exec:17","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:231:        sendAttachment: true, // send attachments/media\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:250:- **sendAttachment**: Send media/files (`to`, `buffer`, `filename`, `asVoice`)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:285:- Inbound attachments are downloaded and stored in the media cache.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/discord.md:303:File attachments:\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/discord.md:1008:OpenClaw can join Discord voice channels for realtime, continuous conversations. This is separate from voice message attachments.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:241:- `resolveSenderNames` (default `true`): when `false`, skip sender profile lookup calls.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/imessage.md:90:    Recommended config when attachments are enabled:\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/imessage.md:338:  <Accordion title=\"Remote attachments fail\">\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/mattermost.md:256:    attachments: [\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/mattermost.md:283:1. Attachments go in `props.attachments`, not top-level `attachments` (silently ignored).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:14:Status: text + DM attachments are supported; channel/group file sending requires `sharePointSiteId` + Graph permissions (see [Sending files in group chats](#sending-files-in-group-chats)). Polls are sent via Adaptive Cards.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:390:- Receive **personal (DM)** file attachments.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:395:- Downloading attachments stored in SharePoint/OneDrive.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:403:- Downloading file attachments stored in SharePoint/OneDrive.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:422:   - `ChannelMessage.Read.All` (channel attachments + history)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:477:- `channels.msteams.sharePointSiteId`: SharePoint site ID for file uploads in group chats/channels (see [Sending files in group chats](#sending-files-in-group-chats)).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:524:- **DMs:** Images and file attachments work via Teams bot file APIs.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:525:- **Channels/groups:** Attachments live in M365 storage (SharePoint/OneDrive). The webhook payload only includes an HTML stub, not the actual file bytes. **Graph API permissions are required** to download channel attachments.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:533:Bots can send files in DMs using the FileConsentCard flow (built-in). However, **sending files in group chats/channels** requires additional setup:\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:543:Bots don't have a personal OneDrive drive (the `/me/drive` Graph API endpoint doesn't work for application identities). To send files in group chats/channels, the bot uploads to a **SharePoint site** and creates a sharing link.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:593:| Group chat + file + `sharePointSiteId` configured | Upload to SharePoint, send sharing link            |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:594:| Group chat + file + no `sharePointSiteId`         | Attempt OneDrive upload (may fail), send text only |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/nostr.md:232:- No media attachments.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/slack.md:259:  <Accordion title=\"Inbound attachments\">\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/slack.md:260:    Slack file attachments are downloaded from Slack-hosted private URLs (token-authenticated request flow) and written to the media store when fetch succeeds and size limits permit.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/slack.md:269:    - file sends use Slack upload APIs and can include thread replies (`thread_ts`)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/synology-chat.md:93:Media sends are supported by URL-based file delivery.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md:897:- `channels.telegram.allowFrom`: DM allowlist (numeric Telegram user IDs). `allowlist` requires at least one sender ID. `open` requires `\"*\"`. `openclaw doctor --fix` can resolve legacy `@username` entries to IDs and can recover allowlist entries from pairing-store files in allowlist migration flows."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":22,"aggregated":"/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:231:        sendAttachment: true, // send attachments/media\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:250:- **sendAttachment**: Send media/files (`to`, `buffer`, `filename`, `asVoice`)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:285:- Inbound attachments are downloaded and stored in the media cache.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/discord.md:303:File attachments:\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/discord.md:1008:OpenClaw can join Discord voice channels for realtime, continuous conversations. This is separate from voice message attachments.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:241:- `resolveSenderNames` (default `true`): when `false`, skip sender profile lookup calls.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/imessage.md:90:    Recommended config when attachments are enabled:\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/imessage.md:338:  <Accordion title=\"Remote attachments fail\">\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/mattermost.md:256:    attachments: [\n/usr/lib/node_modules/ope